    {
      "date": "1996",
      "kind": "designation",
      "description": "Before the city listed it, the Colombo Building had been rated \"3\" in the 1976 citywide architectural inventory and \"B*\" by San Francisco Heritage, and in May 1984 the Landmarks Preservation Advisory Board recommended it for city landmark status — a designation the city did not then make. The State Office of Historic Preservation agreed with the 1982 North Beach survey in 1996 and coded the building \"4S\", meaning it might become eligible for the National Register on its own.",
